{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"ArraySlice","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, one pass, O(V + E): a self-loop is noticed while the search reads the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex’s successors, so a single-vertex component costs nothing more.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The components are those of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stronglyConnectedComponents()"},{"text":" without the trivial ones, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same order, a reverse topological order: every path between two of them goes from a later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one to an earlier one. Each lists its vertices in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order. Empty exactly when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph is acyclic. Each is a slice of one shared array, as in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attractingComponents()"},{"text":", so its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices do not start at 0.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":", so one sort by that vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position puts the components in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order, O(C log C) for C components. On a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"text":", where positions are insertion order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE37nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponentsSays10ArraySliceVy6VertexQzGGyF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ArraySlice","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","modules":[{"name":"Connectivity","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift#L89","fileName":"NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols"},"abstract":[{"text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through both. “Nontrivial” is the model-checking term (a strongly connected component with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at least one edge, as in Büchi-automaton emptiness checks); this is NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"strongly_connected_components"},{"text":" filtered to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"len(c) > 1 or G.has_edge(v, v)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()","title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nontrivialStron